_️ Potential issue_ | _ Critical_

**Logic bug: groups disappear on other instances if any exception exists anywhere.**

You compute groupsWithExceptions from all exceptions across all instances, then hide the group on instances without a matching record. This incorrectly removes base template groups on unrelated instances. Decide inclusion solely by the presence of an instanceException for the current instance.


```diff
-  const [instanceExceptions, allExceptions] = await Promise.all([
+  const [instanceExceptions] = await Promise.all([
     // Exceptions for this specific instance
     ctx.drizzleClient.query.eventVolunteerGroupExceptionsTable.findMany({
       where: and(
         inArray(
           eventVolunteerGroupExceptionsTable.volunteerGroupId,
           volunteerGroupIds,
         ),
         eq(
           eventVolunteerGroupExceptionsTable.recurringEventInstanceId,
           parent.id,
         ),
       ),
     }),
-    // All exceptions for these groups (to determine if they're instance-specific)
-    ctx.drizzleClient.query.eventVolunteerGroupExceptionsTable.findMany({
-      where: inArray(
-        eventVolunteerGroupExceptionsTable.volunteerGroupId,
-        volunteerGroupIds,
-      ),
-      columns: { volunteerGroupId: true },
-    }),
   ]);
@@
-  const instanceExceptionsMap = new Map(
+  const instanceExceptionsMap = new Map(
     instanceExceptions.map((exception) => [
       exception.volunteerGroupId,
       exception,
     ]),
   );
-  // Get set of groups that have any exceptions (instance-specific)
-  const groupsWithExceptions = new Set(
-    allExceptions.map((exception) => exception.volunteerGroupId),
-  );
@@
-  volunteerGroups = volunteerGroups.filter((group) => {
-    const instanceException = instanceExceptionsMap.get(group.id);
-    const hasAnyExceptions = groupsWithExceptions.has(group.id);
-
-    // If group has exceptions (instance-specific), only include if isException: true for this instance
-    if (hasAnyExceptions) {
-      if (instanceException?.isException === true && !instanceException?.deleted) {
-        // Apply exception overrides
-        group.name = instanceException.name ?? group.name;
-        group.description = instanceException.description ?? group.description;
-        group.volunteersRequired =
-          instanceException.volunteersRequired ?? group.volunteersRequired;
-        group.leaderId = instanceException.leaderId ?? group.leaderId;
-
-        (group as { isInstanceException?: boolean }).isInstanceException = true;
-        return true;
-      }
-      return false;
-    }
-    // Template group (no exceptions) - include by default
-    (group as { isInstanceException?: boolean }).isInstanceException = false;
-    return true;
-  });
+  volunteerGroups = volunteerGroups.flatMap((group) => {
+    const ex = instanceExceptionsMap.get(group.id);
+    // If an instance exception exists:
+    if (ex) {
+      if (ex.isException === true && !ex.deleted) {
+        // include with overrides
+        return [{
+          ...group,
+          name: ex.name ?? group.name,
+          description: ex.description ?? group.description,
+          volunteersRequired: ex.volunteersRequired ?? group.volunteersRequired,
+          leaderId: ex.leaderId ?? group.leaderId,
+          isInstanceException: true,
+          recurringEventInstanceId: parent.id,
+        }];
+      }
+      // exclude for this instance when explicitly deleted/not participating
+      return [];
+    }
+    // No instance exception: include base template group as-is
+    return [{ ...group, isInstanceException: false, recurringEventInstanceId: parent.id }];
+  });
```


Also applies to: 92-116

<details>
<summary> Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In src/graphql/types/Event/volunteerGroups.ts around lines 92-116 and 130-161,
the filter logic uses a global groupsWithExceptions set (exceptions across all
instances) which causes template groups to be hidden on instances that have no
instance-specific exception; change the logic to base inclusion solely on
whether an instanceException exists for the current instance: remove or ignore
the groupsWithExceptions.has(group.id) check, treat absence of instanceException
as a template group (include it), and only apply the instanceException overrides
and return false when an instanceException exists and is marked deleted or
isException is false for this instance; ensure you still set isInstanceException
true when applying overrides and false when including the template group.
```

</details>

